 The Milwaukee Brewers celebrate winning the Fall Classic in St. Petersburg, Fla., last night. Photo: Kelly Gavin/MLB Photos via Getty Images ⚾️  The World Series champion  Milwaukee Brewers dominated baseball this year in "so many ways," The Athletic writes: 103 regular-season wins, a 16-2 record over their last 18 regular-season games, a postseason sweep against the defending champion L.A. Dodgers, and more. Gift link . 🔎 A federal investigation of Rep. Ilhan Omar (D-Minn.) "is focused in part on whether she entered into a sham marriage in 2009 to help a man suspected of being her brother obtain a green card," The New York Times reports. Gift link . 📈 The U.S. economy grew 3.4% in the third quarter, according to government data out today. The economy, supercharged by AI investment and consumer spending, enters the final stretch of the year with remarkable momentum despite the Iran war and high energy prices. More from Courtenay Brown . 🏈 An estimated 75% of ex-NFL players who died between 2008 and 2023 had the brain disease CTE, a new study finds. The league told ESPN that it "continuously strives to make the game of football safer, including by implementing strategies to reduce concussions and head impacts." Go deeper . 
 
