 4. 🥣 1 for the road: Cheerios + Ziploc 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: General Mills General Mills is rolling out Cheerios boxes with built-in Ziploc bags to help keep the cereal fresh, Axios Twin Cities' Nick Halter reports. 

 The company, based in the Minneapolis suburb of Golden Valley, said it received hundreds of thousands of letters, emails and DMs asking for an easier way to reseal a cereal box. So General Mills teamed up with Ziploc. The new Cheerios and Honey Nut Cheerios boxes are currently a Walmart.com exclusive , but they'll roll out to national retailers in the coming months. 

